# The Stars Who Forgot to Shine

In the beginning, the night sky was empty and dark. The Moon ruled alone, cold and distant, casting pale light upon the sleeping world below.

The Sky Weaver created thousands of stars to keep the Moon company, scattering them across the heavens like seeds. But these first stars were timid and afraid. They hid their light inside themselves, remaining dark and invisible.

The Moon grew lonely and called out to them. "Why do you hide? You were made to illuminate the darkness!"

The stars trembled. "We are too small," they whispered. "Our light is weak. What difference can we make against such vast darkness?"

